  "provider_query": "Python standard library documentation for the venv module",
  "answer": "Relevant sources for the Python standard library `venv` module:\n\n1. **Official library reference (Python 3.14)** — `venv` creates lightweight virtual environments on a base Python install (added in 3.3). Covers `python -m venv`, CLI flags (`--system-site-packages`, `--symlinks`, `--clear`, `--upgrade`, `--without-pip`, `--upgrade-deps`, etc.), and the `EnvBuilder` API.  \n   https://docs.python.org/3.14/library/venv.html\n\n2. **Stable docs index (latest 3.x)** — Same module page under the current stable docs tree.  \n   https://docs.python.org/3/library/venv.html\n\n3. **Tutorial: Virtual Environments and Packages** — Official walkthrough of creating and activating a venv (`.venv` convention, Windows `Scripts\\activate`, Unix `source bin/activate`).  \n   https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/venv.html\n\n4. **Development docs tutorial** — Same tutorial on the in-progress docs branch.  \n   https://docs.python.org/dev/tutorial/venv.html\n\n5. **CPython source: `Lib/venv/`** — Implementation of the module (PEP 405), including `EnvBuilder`.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/main/Lib/venv\n\n6. **CPython `Lib/venv/__init__.py`** — Source of the CLI help text and environment creation logic.  \n   https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Lib/venv/__init__.py\n\n7. **PEP 405 — Python Virtual Environments** — Design document the module is based on.  \n   https://peps.python.org/pep-0405/\n\n8. **pydevtools handbook summary** — Concise overview of stdlib `venv` vs `virtualenv`/`uv`, maintenance status, and common create commands.  \n   https://pydevtools.com/handbook/reference/venv/",
